{"type":"assistant","message":{"model":"claude-opus-5","id":"msg_bdrk_pa6k4nkn2mthfo4nby6ta7achu4xh3u6mubui6gmrptza4pss76q","type":"message","role":"assistant","content":[{"type":"text","text":"**Verification complete — all four phases pass across all 48 build configurations.**\n\n## Results\n\n| gate | result |\n|---|---|\n| `cargo check` for every feature combo | 48/48 OK, 0 warnings |\n| `nm -D` symbol parity (C ⊆ Rust) | 48/48, **0 missing**; 0 undefined non-libc |\n| Phase B — all 48 `CONFIGS.md` rows | pass, **2424 test cases**, 0 failures |\n| Phase C — all 11 `ERRORS.md` rows | pass |\n| KAT driver digest, C vs Rust | 48/48 **MATCH** |\n\n## Bugs found and fixed in the Rust\n\n1. **No FFI struct was `#[repr(C)]`** — `spx_ctx`, `blakestate256/512`, `leaf_info_x1`, `fors_gen_leaf_info`, `AES_XOF_struct`. Confirmed live miscompare: `blake256_compress` wrote `h` at byte 64 instead of 0, and rustc reordered `leaf_info_x1`'s pointers ahead of `wots_sign_leaf`.\n2. **`rng.c` was only partially translated at the export level** — `DRBG_ctx`, `AES256_ECB`, `AES256_CTR_DRBG_Update`, `seedexpander`, `seedexpander_init` had no exports, and the DRBG lived in a private `Mutex` so the C-visible global didn't exist; `seedexpander` couldn't even express its `x == NULL` rejection. `src/rng.rs` was rebuilt around a `#[repr(C)] #[no_mangle] pub static mut DRBG_ctx`.\n3. **`cst` missing** — `blake512.c` declares its round-constant table non-`static`, so it is in `.dynsym`; added as `#[no_mangle] pub static cst`.\n4. **`gen_message_random` (blake) wrote too few bytes** — the C does `blakeX_final(&S, R)`, i.e. 32/64 bytes into `R`, not `SPX_N`.\n5. **`crypto_sign_verify` built a slice from an unvalidated `siglen`** before the `siglen != SPX_BYTES` check.\n\n## Notable C behaviour replicated, not \"fixed\"\n\n`hash_blake.c` passes **byte** counts to `blakeX_update`, which expects **bit** counts. For short messages the BLAKE state never fills a block, `blakeX_final` compresses nothing, and the message therefore has no influence on the signature. The error-path tests assert C/Rust *agreement* here and reach the rejection path via a long message instead.\n\n## Environment note\n\n`rng.c` needs OpenSSL headers, absent from `/usr/include`. `verif/build_c_all.sh` locates a nix-store OpenSSL and a system `libcrypto.so.3` and injects them through CMake flag variables, so `libsphincs_core_det.so` and `driver` build for all 48 configurations. Using the *deterministic* core is what makes `crypto_sign_keypair` / `crypto_sign_signature` byte-comparable. `c_src` is unmodified.\n\nArtifacts: `translation/{SYMBOLS,ERRORS,CONFIGS}.md`, `translation/tests/diff_*.rs`, `verif/*.sh` (see `verif/README.md`)."}],"stop_reason":null,"stop_sequence":null,"stop_details":null,"usage":{"input_tokens":2,"cache_creation_input_tokens":580,"cache_read_input_tokens":459531,"cache_creation":{"ephemeral_5m_input_tokens":580,"ephemeral_1h_input_tokens":0},"output_tokens":1,"service_tier":"standard"},"context_management":null},"parent_tool_use_id":null,"session_id":"6f585a29-7725-4f54-ba8d-bf3ce186bd20","uuid":"a0a79f66-265f-4057-a3e6-2f3287771787","timestamp":"2026-08-29T16:22:07.176Z"}
